      "id": "DR-1",
      "date": "2026-10-04",
      "status": "CLOSED 2026-10-05",
      "question": "D-neg flags bd03 p4 (CMMI10) and p6 (CMSY10). Are these pages maths under the maths rule?",
      "evidence": "run_detection.py --run D-neg, output/detection.json. p6 draws the multiplication sign in CMSY10 inside chlorophyll formulas of the form 'Chl a (mg/mL) = 0.0127 x A663 - 0.0027 x A645'; p4 draws glyphs in CMMI10 next to '3 +'. Page images: output/.pages/bd03/p004.png, p006.png. bd01 and bd02: 0 flagged. D-neg update 2026-10-04: pc01 (prose-only control) 0/24 flagged; D-neg total 2 of 67 pages.",
      "consequence": "If maths: bd03 is not maths-free, the 'no_maths by construction' assumption fails, and the negative-control set needs an amendment (label bd03 pages, or replace bd03). If not maths: a detector false positive, and the failure rule applies (fix in the implementation worktree, bump MATHS_DETECTOR_VERSION, rerun D-neg).",
      "decision": "Option 1: label all bd01-bd03 pages, amend G1 to count only pages labelled no_maths",
      "outcome": "Operator labelled bd03 p4 and p6 maths (p6 note: chemical equation). Both flags are true positives; G1 passes under A1."
    },
    {
      "id": "DR-2",
      "date": "2026-10-04",
      "status": "DECIDED",
      "question": "Word + Cambria Math slot: 1106.0083v2 (Lin) is Word 2007 but its equations use Symbol and MT Extra, not Cambria Math.",
      "decision": "Use the approved backup 2002.10527v1 (mp05, Word 2010, CambriaMath embedded). Keep mp02 on disk as a recorded rejection.",
      "finding": "Word papers whose equations come from MathType or Equation Editor 3.0 use Symbol / MT Extra, which the maths list does not include. The detector cannot see that maths. Report it beside the unmatched-font list in 7.2; it is outside the experiment sets."
    },
    {
      "id": "DR-3",
      "date": "2026-10-05",
      "status": "DECIDED",
      "question": "How to score pages with no output in Q4 recall?",
      "decision": "Report two views: 'all' (a page with no output scores 0.0) and 'with_output'. Chosen before PaddleOCR-VL finished; the protocol did not say.",
      "applies_to": "score_recall.py"
    },
    {
      "id": "DR-4",
      "date": "2026-10-05",
      "status": "DECIDED before results were seen",
      "question": "Which pages form each engine's noise list (G3)? The protocol says the operator marks noise but not how pages are chosen for review.",
      "decision": "Automatic screen, then operator review. Reference = pypdf text layer (E-maths) or Experiment 33 transcription, all text (E-scan). Engine prose = Markdown minus formulas, HTML tags and image links. Tokens = Experiment 33 tokens(). Listed when unsupported tokens >= 10 and >= 15 % of engine tokens, or a 20+ character line repeats 3+ times. Plus 5 unflagged audit pages per engine (seed 37) to check the screen. Pages with no output are reported, not reviewed.",
      "applies_to": "make_noise_review.py",
      "limits": "Formulas are not screened (maths fonts drop symbols from the text layer); invented formulas are caught only by the operator on listed pages.",
      "amendment_2026-10-05": "After the first screen: io06 p53 (named in protocol.md as Experiment 34 bleed-through noise) is added to the list for every engine with output. The screen missed it because dots-mocr emitted only 10 tokens there. Thresholds unchanged; audit draw unchanged (taken before the addition). Finding: the token screen cannot see noise on near-blank pages.",
      "amendment_2026-10-05b": "Operator decision during Gate D: on every page that is on either engine's list (21 pages), every engine with output gets a verdict ('paired'). 23 verdicts became 41 (dots-mocr 21, paddleocr-vl 20; paddleocr-vl has no output on io06:53). Gives a paired comparison on the same pages and shows the screen's misses. Earlier verdict slots unchanged."
